     "role": "assistant",
     "content": "**New Feature: Daily Ticket Summaries for Slack**\n\nHi there,\n\nStarting your day buried in the support queue? Not anymore.\n\nWe're excited to launch **Daily Digest for Slack** — a simple new integration that posts a clear, skimmable summary of your open support tickets to a Slack channel of your choice, every morning.\n\nBuilt for busy support teams, it's the easiest way to keep everyone aligned without living in the helpdesk.\n\n**What you get**\n\nEvery weekday morning at the time you choose, you'll get an automated post with:\n\n* Total open tickets, broken down by status and priority\n* New tickets since yesterday\n* Tickets at risk of breaching SLA\n* Your 5 oldest unresolved tickets, with direct links\n\nNo digging. No manual reports. Just the context you need to prioritize, right where your team already works.\n\n**Why you'll love it**\n\nCustomers in our beta told us it changed their standups. Support leads spot bottlenecks faster, agents know what to tackle first, and stakeholders outside support — like product and success — finally have visibility without needing another login.\n\n**How to turn it on**\n\nIt takes less than 2 minutes:\n\n1. Go to **Settings > Integrations > Slack** and click Connect\n2. Choose the channel where you want the digest (we recommend #support-daily)\n3. Pick your delivery time and timezone\n\nThat's it. Your first digest will arrive tomorrow morning.\n\nDaily Digest for Slack is available now on all plans at no extra cost.\n\nTry it this week and let us know what you think — just reply to this email or reach out via chat. We built this for you, and your feedback shapes what's next.\n\nThanks for being a customer,\n\nThe Team",
